# fastboot-meowarch install hook

post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
fastboot-meowarch: the commands are `fastboot-m` (short) and `fastboot-meowarch`
  (alias) — both are symlinks to the same binary. The distro's android-tools
  `fastboot` is left untouched, so both packages can be installed side by side.
  USB works like platform-tools; if `fastboot-m devices` is empty but `lsusb`
  sees the phone, install udev rules (AUR: android-udev) or run as root.
  mke2fs/make_f2fs/mke2fs.conf live in /usr/lib/fastboot-meowarch/ and are
  found automatically by the fastboot binary (same-directory lookup).
EOF
}